{"skill":{"slug":"mac-tts","displayName":"Mac TTS"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769585143301,"changelog":"Initial release: macOS say command for text-to-speech","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1680,"sha256":"eba20b0888c528895b868f187e84be6d6d230b7cd0d5f01f2f10b958fd5f2c74","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1734,"sha256":"812ed0735535509e5c61a41b4e3af8289813c0ea494d51e7b25b6739c3e36522","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022544503,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b9612b3bd2b6396aefa57c88a1aeeebdc9361bc428842c6c9806adbec9ce0e18","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b9612b3bd2b6396aefa57c88a1aeeebdc9361bc428842c6c9806adbec9ce0e18","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: mac-tts\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It uses standard macOS commands (`say` for text-to-speech and `osascript` for volume control) for their intended purposes. The `SKILL.md` provides clear, non-malicious instructions and examples for using these commands, without any evidence of prompt injection attempts, data exfiltration, malicious execution, or persistence mechanisms.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160186750},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789022544503},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a simple macOS text-to-speech helper with disclosed local audio commands and no hidden data access, persistence, or network behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill is macOS-specific and includes `osascript` examples that can change local output volume or unmute audio, which is disclosed and proportionate for audible notifications.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package contains a single Markdown skill file with no executable scripts, dependencies, installers, or remote payload retrieval.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are straightforward examples for speaking text, selecting voices, listing voices, and adjusting volume; there are no role changes, prompt overrides, hidden conditions, or unrelated tasks.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence, credential access, privilege escalation, background services, or cross-session modifications are present; the optional async `say ... &` example is user-directed and limited to speech playback.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is to use macOS text-to-speech, and the artifact only documents the built-in `say` command plus optional system volume checks and adjustments.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you want Codex to speak messages through a Mac's speakers. Be aware that the examples include changing or unmuting system volume, so use it in an environment where audible output is appropriate.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022544503}}}}}